"""Authoritative Power & Utilities system decomposition (modules) + extra use cases.

Hand-authored, domain-accurate catalog that REPLACES the keyword-derived asset
list. Taxonomy: each source_category is a deployed platform/system; modules are
the vendor-neutral capabilities/subsystems within it. ADMS is the integrated
DISTRIBUTION platform; EMS the integrated TRANSMISSION platform; standalone
SCADA/OMS are represented as their own thin categories so utilities that run
them separately map cleanly. `domain` (owning LOB) disambiguates capabilities
that appear in both (e.g. SCADA under EMS=Transmission vs ADMS=Distribution).

Each module: (source_category, module, keywords, sub_vertical, owning_domain, effort)
  keywords -> match the parent-catalog's free-text dataRequirements so the 198
  imported use cases still resolve their required data. New use cases below use
  EXPLICIT (category, module) requires — no keyword guessing.
"""

